@startuml
skinparam dpi 200
skinparam defaultFontName "Segoe UI, Arial, sans-serif"

<style>
sequenceDiagram {
  participant {
    Padding 30
    Margin 20
  }
}
</style>

skinparam defaultFontSize 20
skinparam sequenceGroupFontSize 20
skinparam sequenceReferenceFontSize 18
skinparam arrowFontSize 18
skinparam noteFontSize 17
skinparam participantFontSize 20
skinparam actorFontSize 20

skinparam maxMessageSize 400
skinparam wrapWidth 400
skinparam roundCorner 8
skinparam shadowing false

skinparam sequenceLifeLineBorderColor #2C3E50
skinparam sequenceGroupBorderColor #C0392B
skinparam sequenceGroupHeaderFontStyle bold

autonumber

actor "Traveler / Adversary\n[Client Browser]" as B #EBF5FB
participant "Fastify 5 BFF API\n[Session Boundary]" as API #E8F8F5
database "PostgreSQL Database\n[app_security schema]" as DB #FEF9E7
participant "Directus Studio / Admin\n[Identity Security Admin]" as ADM #FADBD8

== Scenario 1: Event-Driven Revocation via Database Trigger ==

ADM -> DB: Identity mutation event\n(Suspend account / reset password / reconfigure MFA)
activate DB

note over DB #FADBD8
  <b>PostgreSQL Database Trigger Fires:</b>
  Trigger detects mutation on user identity table.
  Synchronously revokes all active sessions belonging to affected user:
  revoked_at <- CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, revoke_reason <- event_code
  (Executed atomically within same database transaction).
end note
DB --> ADM: Transaction committed (All active sessions invalidated)
deactivate DB

B -> API: Request with previously issued cookie
activate API
API -> DB: Lookup active session by SHA-256(handle)
activate DB
DB --> API: Record found but session is flagged as revoked
deactivate DB
API --> B: HTTP 401 Unauthorized\n(Evict client session cookie: Max-Age=0)
deactivate API

== Scenario 2: Token Reuse Anomaly & Entire Family Annihilation ==

B -> API: Adversary replays old rotated handle\n(Replay Attack)
activate API
API -> DB: Query session state by SHA-256(handle)
activate DB
DB --> API: Handle matches rotated ancestor (Token Reuse Anomaly!)
deactivate DB

API -> DB: Annihilate entire session family lineage\n(Revoke all sessions sharing session_family_id)
activate DB
API -> DB: Record security violation in audit log\n(auth.session_revalidation, denied)
DB --> API: Entire session genealogical tree terminated
deactivate DB

API --> B: HTTP 401 Unauthorized (Adversary locked out, cookie evicted)
deactivate API

note over B, API #FCF3CF
  <b>Defense-in-Depth Guarantee:</b>
  Replay of a previously rotated token indicates credential theft.
  The system annihilates the entire session lineage, preventing unauthorized access.
end note

@enduml
